From d7a9f34a453efad05eec9a30244ebd81446520a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 04:12:25 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 29/50] render: parallax and camera the way Wallpaper Engine
 does

Decoded from wallpaper64.exe 2.8.485: the camera update (GH 0x1401b8af0),
the per-object offset in the scene render loop (GH 0x1401b9b50), the shake
(GH 0x1401c7680), the zoom in the scene tick (GH 0x1401afbf0) and the
scene constructor's defaults (GH 0x1401b6c60).

Mouse parallax. `cameraparallaxdelay` was read as a bool (0.1 -> k = 0:
parallax never moved in 14 of the owner's 25 parallax scenes). Now, while
`cameraparallax` is on (read every frame), the target is
  W * (0.5 (1 - infl) + mx infl), H * (0.5 (1 - infl) + (1 - my) infl)
with the pointer clamped to 0..1 (y up), plus the camera position (the
shake). A delay <= 0 snaps to it, otherwise
  k = min (1, (1 - delay / 3) * 10 * dt), pos += (target - pos) k.
The position starts at the scene centre. Each object is translated in the
world by (root.origin - pos) * cameraparallaxamount * root.parallaxDepth,
root being its topmost ancestor, so depth 0 stays put and a subtree moves
as one. Off = no offset (it used to keep the last one). It was
(depth + amount) * the raw cursor * amount * influence * W. CParticle's
0.65 minimum depth is gone. parallaxDepth defaults to 1 1, as in WE, and
every object (groups too) has one.

g_ParallaxPosition is fed: the smoothed position over the scene size,
clamped to 0..1, 0.5 0.5 at the start (uniform 0x72, GH 0x14010a0e0).

Camera. general.zoom scales the view about the scene centre, times the
zoom of the active camera object (the last visible one whose parents are
visible; `"camera": "default"` objects were "unknown"). camerashake moves
the camera by (cos t, sin 1.333 t), t = speed^2 * g_Time, its length raised
to roughness^3 (unless that is <= 0.001 or 1), times amplitude * 0.01 *
the scene height. fov/nearz/farz are read from `general` (they were read
from `camera`, which has none); the 2D projection keeps its 0..1000 depth.
The parallax defaults (amount 0.5, delay 0.1, influence 0.5) and the shake
defaults (speed 3, amplitude 0.5, roughness 1) are WE's.

Not done: a camera object's origin (pan) -- the library's scenes
disagree on whether it is relative to the scene centre; the camera paths;
g_EffectTextureProjectionMatrix; text objects (CText) ignore the parallax
offset.

Origin: ours
Why: mouse parallax was dead in 14 of 25 scenes and off-centre in the rest; zoom, camera shake and camera objects were ignored (docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md B5: G10-G12, G14/E1, G15-G19)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01288H8a42pVTGcB74tx4LjJ
